"13">No</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Bank_note" title="Bank note">Noteable</a></th><td colspan="13">Yes</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Choose_Option" title="Choose Option">Options</a></th><td colspan="13">Drop</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Examine" title="Examine">Examine</a></th><td colspan="13">Useful for catching really big fish.</td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><th colspan="20" class="infobox-subheader">Values</th></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Value" title="Value">Value</a></th><td colspan="13">5 coins</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/High_Level_Alchemy" title="High Level Alchemy">High alch</a></th><td colspan="13">3 coins</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Low_Level_Alchemy" title="Low Level Alchemy">Low alch</a></th><td colspan="13">2 coins</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Weight" title="Weight">Weight</a></th><td colspan="13">1.36 kg</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Item_respawns" class="mw-redirect" title="Item respawns">Respawn time</a></th><td colspan="13">100 ticks (60 seconds)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><th colspan="20" class="infobox-subheader">Grand Exchange</th></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/RuneScape:Grand_Exchange_Market_Watch" title="RuneScape:Grand Exchange Market Watch">Exchange</a></th><td colspan="13"><span class="infobox-quantity" data-val-each="150"><span class="infobox-quantity-replace">150</span> coins (<a href="/w/Exchange:Harpoon" title="Exchange:Harpoon">info</a>)</span></td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Grand_Exchange#Buy_limits" title="Grand Exchange">Buy limit</a></th><td colspan="13">40</td></tr><tr><th colspan="7"><a href="/w/Grand_Exchange#Volume" title="Grand Exchange">Daily volume</a></th><td colspan="13">995</td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-full-width-content"><div class="realtime-prices plainlinks"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://prices.runescape.wiki/osrs/item/311"><span class="cdx-button realtime-ge-openbtn" style="font-size:inherit;min-height:0;padding:3px 12px">View real-time prices</span></a></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-full-width-content"><div class="GEChartBox"><div class="GEChartItems" style="display:none"></div><div class="GEdatachart smallChart" style="height:160px;margin:0 auto;width:258px"><div style="user-select:none;opacity:.75;text-align:center;font-size:.9em">Loading...</div></div><div class="GEdataprices" data-item="Harpoon" data-itemid="311" data-limit="40" data-value="5" style="display:none"></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr class="advanced-data"><th colspan="20" class="infobox-subheader">Advanced data</th></tr><tr class="advanced-data"><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr class="advanced-data"><th colspan="7">Item ID</th><td colspan="13">311</td></tr><tr class="advanced-data"><th colspan="7">Link</th><td colspan="13"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://chisel.weirdgloop.org/moid/item_id.html#311">MOID</a></td></tr><tr class="advanced-data"><td colspan="20" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr></tbody></table>
<figure class="mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File"><a href="/w/File:Harpoon_detail.png" class="mw-file-description"><img src="/images/thumb/Harpoon_detail.png/90px-Harpoon_detail.png?73012" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="90" height="120" class="mw-file-element" srcset="/images/thumb/Harpoon_detail.png/180px-Harpoon_detail.png?73012 2x" data-file-width="1106" data-file-height="1478" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>
<p>A <b>harpoon</b> is an item used to catch certain types of <a href="/w/Fish" title="Fish">fish</a>, as part of the <a href="/w/Fishing" title="Fishing">Fishing</a> skill. It can be used to catch <a href="/w/Raw_tuna" title="Raw tuna">tuna</a> at level 35, <a href="/w/Raw_swordfish" title="Raw swordfish">swordfish</a> at level 50, and <a href="/w/Raw_shark" title="Raw shark">sharks</a> at level 76. Swordfish and tuna can be caught at <a href="/w/Fishing_spot_(cage,_harpoon)" title="Fishing spot (cage, harpoon)">cage/harpoon</a> fishing spots, while sharks can be caught at <a href="/w/Fishing_spot_(big_net,_harpoon)" title="Fishing spot (big net, harpoon)">big net/harpoon</a> spots. Harpoons are also used when fighting <a href="/w/Tempoross" title="Tempoross">Tempoross</a>, to catch <a href="/w/Harpoonfish" title="Harpoonfish">harpoonfish</a> and fish from the <a href="/w/Spirit_pool" title="Spirit pool">spirit pools</a> that weaken the boss.
</p><p>Harpoons can be purchased from most <a href="/w/Fishing_shops" title="Fishing shops">fishing shops</a> and can be stored in a <a href="/w/Tackle_box" title="Tackle box">tackle box</a>.
</p><p>For <a href="/w/Pay-to-play" class="mw-redirect" title="Pay-to-play">pay-to-play</a> players, several other types of harpoons exist. The <a href="/w/Barb-tail_harpoon" title="Barb-tail harpoon">barb-tail harpoon</a> is wieldable, allowing saving one inventory space over an ordinary harpoon. The <a href="/w/Dragon_harpoon" title="Dragon harpoon">dragon harpoon</a> is also wieldable, has a 20% increased catch rate compared to other harpoons, and has a special attack that boosts <a href="/w/Fishing" title="Fishing">Fishing</a> level by 3, but requires 61 <a href="/w/Fishing" title="Fishing">Fishing</a> to use and 60 <a href="/w/Attack" title="Attack">Attack</a> to wield. The <a href="/w/Crystal_harpoon" title="Crystal harpoon">crystal harpoon</a> is an improved version of the <a href="/w/Dragon_harpoon" title="Dragon harpoon">dragon harpoon</a>, with a 35% increased catch rate and increased requirements to use.
</p><p>Alternately, pay-to-play players who learn <a href="/w/Barbarian_Training#Fishing" title="Barbarian Training">barbarian fishing</a> can forego a harpoon entirely by learning how to barehand fish.
</p>
